{
  "summary": "Removes the `-persistmempoolv1` command-line option and stops support for writing legacy non-XORed `mempool.dat` files on shutdown or via `savemempool`. Reading existing v1 mempool files remains supported to allow seamless upgrades from old versions. The PR also updates `mempool_compatibility.py` to test against v31.0 and adds a test case for importing malformed mempool dumps.",
  "problem": "The `-persistmempoolv1` option was introduced as a temporary fallback to allow users to downgrade to v26.x or earlier, which could not read XOR-obfuscated `mempool.dat` files. Because v26 and earlier releases have reached end-of-life, the fallback option is unnecessary technical debt.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: \"-persistmempoolv1 was added in #28207 as a temporary option to allow downgrading to v26 and earlier, which can't read the XOR'ed mempool.dat. v26 has now been EOL for a while... docs have always stated that this was a 'temporary option that will be removed in the future'.\"",
    "Existing help text in src/init.cpp explicitly noted: \"This temporary option will be removed in the future.\""
  ],
